                <pb facs="0701" n="621" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg621"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Powell to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-08-05"><hi rendition="#italic">August 5,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Powell reports that Firmin set up a new government on August 4 at Gonaives,
                    known as the provisional government of Artibonite and the northwest, with Firmin
                    as President; Killick as secretary of the navy and secretary of war; Bourand as
                    secretary of the treasury; Henriquez as principal secretary of state for foreign
                    affairs; St. Louis as secretary of public works; Chicoye as secretary of the
                    interior; and Lamour as secretary of agriculture.</p>
                <p>Admiral Killick is to leave on August 5 for Cape Haitien.)</p>
            </div>
